INTRODUCTION T O THE SELF
Chapter One defined ¡ as any words said by any character to
anyone. This traf fic of talk runs along three distinct avenues: said to others,
said to a reader or ©, an d said to oneself. The chapter that follows
focuses ¯ latter two tracks: direct address to Ó and inner
¡ between selves. Altho ugh the stage and screen limit  the use of
these two modes, · ßis t and short-story writer , they are  the stuf f of
