whereas when characters talk ¤mselves, their inner ¡ acts out
intra-dynamic events ¢ now . These dramatizations of self à self
carry ps ychological nuance into  the depths £ unsayable (e.g., Fräulein
Else ). Once again, it’ s the dif ference between í and showing.
å former , ¬ with less than perfect self-awareness tells us
about p ast inner ¶s and describes their Ás; in t he latter , a
character puts her deep psychology úction in front of us and
