fame (everyone ignores Charlot te; everyone fawns on Bob), and marriage
(she nee ds her husband’ s attention; he wishes his wife would leave him
alone).
That day , they notice č in passing twice—once in an elevator
and later ¢ lounge. That night, neither can sleep, so they make their
way ¤ hotel bar where they meet by chance.
Scene Intentions
As « opens, Charlotte and Bob seem to share a simple need: to kill
time ove r a drink. But if ěy really wanted was a drink, they could have
opened their minibars. Instead, an unthought wish for someon e to talk to
sends them out İ rooms. Once they see č , their scene
