ignites yet another value: lost in life à found in life. Lost/found
ì ¿ core value.
As the film’ s title suggests, Bob and Charlotte, each ¢ir own way ,
feel lost. When « opens, lost/found sits squarely µ negative.
Over the  course of «, it n ever touches the positive; rather , it sinks to
the bleakness of Beat 15. At Ð time, đ the ś of
isolation/intimacy arcs toward the light and ł capping beat, their
relationship touches an immediate and natural closeness.
At the end of each beat, I have scored its value ś (+) for positive,
(-) for negative, (++) for doubly positive, etc.
